  "fsw_exports": [],
  "description": "A 300 kg satellite built in the 3D model editor: an octagonal bus, two solar panels, a dish, a star tracker and, inside, a battery off to one side. Its mass, center of mass, inertia, drag and sunlight surfaces and Vizard look all come from the model. Sun-safe pointing, wheels only; three orbits.\n\nWhat to look at:\n- Spacecraft > Edit... > 3D model: the center of mass is 4.8 cm toward +x and 6.3 cm toward -z of B, the bus's centre; a product of inertia (Ixz 6.3 kg m^2) turns two principal axes 19 deg.\n- octa-sat.rw_speeds: up to 850 RPM in the turn to the Sun, then rw-y drifts about -2.1 RPM an orbit: sunlight pushes 4.8 cm off the center of mass, and no torque rods unload the wheels.\n- octa-sat.sun_heading_body: within 0.1 deg of the Sun after 7 min.\n\nTry changing:\n- The battery's position x to 0 (Open 3D model editor...): the center of mass moves to 0.8 cm from B, and rw-y ends near +0.9 RPM instead of -6.5. At x = -0.3 m it drifts the other way, to +8.3 RPM.\n- The bus Shell instead of Solid: Ixx grows from 134 to 172 kg m^2.\n- Import .obj... in the editor, for your own model.\n\nNote:\n- Parts do not shade each other, and the panels are fixed to the body.",
  "schema_version": 4
}
